/**
 * @page topic_packet_types ACIP Packet Types
 * @ingroup module_network
 * @brief The current packet families and their dispatch rules.
 *
 * Packet types live in `include/ascii-chat/network/packet/packet.h`. The packet
 * header carries type, length, client identity, and CRC. Transport adapters
 * frame bytes; ACIP handlers validate and dispatch the packet above them.
 *
 * @section packet_families Families
 *
 * - Handshake and rekey: protocol version, crypto capabilities/parameters,
 *   key exchange, authentication, encrypted records, and epoch transitions.
 * - Control: capabilities, ping/pong, join/leave, stream start/stop, server
 *   state, size updates, errors, and remote logs.
 * - Media: ASCII frames, image frames, H.264/H.265 frames, audio batches, and
 *   Opus audio batches.
 * - ACDS: session creation/join/leave, signaling, participant state, host
 *   designation, ring consensus, quality, and discovery errors.
 *
 * `PACKET_TYPE_AUDIO` is retained as a legacy compatibility type. New media
 * code should use `PACKET_TYPE_AUDIO_BATCH` or `PACKET_TYPE_AUDIO_OPUS_BATCH`.
 * `PACKET_TYPE_ENCRYPTED` is an envelope, not an application media type.
 *
 * @section packet_rules Classification
 *
 * The ACIP message helpers classify control, media, signaling, and precompressed
 * packets. Handshake packets are handled before the session reaches READY;
 * encrypted records and rekey packets have explicit epoch rules. Do not add a
 * packet type just to move bytes between a producer and transport: use an
 * existing ACIP message or extend the protocol handler and validation together.
 *
 * @section packet_api APIs
 *
 * Use `packet_send_via_transport()` or the type-specific helpers in
 * `network/acip/client.h`, `server.h`, and `send.h`. Direct socket helpers are
 * backend-level compatibility APIs and must not be used by application modes.
 * Receive paths validate the header, length, magic, CRC, security state, and
 * packet family before invoking the handler.
 *
 * @see topic_network
 * @see topic_av
 * @see include/ascii-chat/network/packet/packet.h
 */
